<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry II of Castile</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1334–1379</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Henry of Trastámara</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry II was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> from 1369 to 1379, an illegitimate son of Alfonso XI. He led a civil war against his half-brother Peter I with French and Aragonese support, was defeated at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najera">Nájera</a> in 1367, and killed Peter after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-montiel">Battle of Montiel</a> in 1369. He founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-trastamara">House of Trastámara</a>, which later ruled Castile and Aragon.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-ii-of-castile.jpg" alt="Henry II of Castile" width="224" height="316" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jaume Serra · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Enrique_II_de_Castilla.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
